title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.3, Revision 6

- Reserve Tokens for:
 * SPV_INTEL_media_block_io
 * SPV_NV_cooperative_matrix
 * SPV_INTEL_device_side_avc_motion_estimation, partially. See the SPV_INTEL_device_side_avc_motion_estimation
   extension specification for a full listing of tokens.

- Fixed Issues:
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #406: <<Scope_-id-, Scope>> values must come from the table of scope values.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #419: <<Validation, Validation rules>> include *AtomicCounter* in the list of
   storage classes allowed for pointer operands to an *OpFunctionCall*.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #325: <<OpPhi, *OpPhi*>> clarifications regarding parent dominance, in the
   instruction and the <<Validation, validation rules>>, and forward references in the
   <<LogicalLayout, Logical Layout section>>.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #415: Remove the non-writable storage classes *PushConstant* and *Input*
   from the *FPRoundingMode* decoration <<ShaderValidation, shader validation rule>>.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #404: Clarify when <<OpGroupNonUniformShuffleXor, *OpGroupNonUniformShuffleXor*>>,
   <<OpGroupNonUniformShuffleUp, *OpGroupNonUniformShuffleUp*>>, and
   <<OpGroupNonUniformShuffleDown, *OpGroupNonUniformShuffleDown*>> are valid or result in undefined values.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #393: Be more clear that <<OpConvertUToPtr, *OpConvertUToPtr*>>
   and <<OpConvertPtrToU, *OpConvertPtrToU*>> operate only on unsigned scalar integers.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #416: Result are undefined for all <<Bit, Shift instructions>> for shifts amounts
   equal to the bit width of the operand.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #399: Refine the definition of a <<VariablePointer, variable pointer>>,
   particularly for function parameters receiving a variable pointer.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #441: Clarify that <<Atomic, atomic instruction's>> _Scope <id>_ must be a valid memory scope.
   More generally, all _Scope <id>_ operands are now either _Memory_ or _Execution_.
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #426: Be more direct about undefined behavior for non-uniform control flow in
   <<OpControlBarrier, *OpControlBarrier*>> and the <<OpGroupAsyncCopy, *OpGroup...*>> instructions that discuss this.

- Deprecate
 * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #429: Deprecate <<OpDecorationGroup, *OpDecorationGroup*>>,
   <<OpGroupDecorate, *OpGroupDecorate*>>, and <<OpGroupMemberDecorate, *OpGroupMemberDecorate*>>

- Editorial
 * Add more clarity that the full <<ClientAPI, client API describes the execution environment>>
  (there is not a separate specification from the client API specification).
